60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate D, the Mobile Branch, faces serious risks from winter road closures and delivery delays.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Candidate D directly addresses the bus link loss in the outer wards, which is critical for access.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"Candidate A, Language Circles, relies on grant funding that expires after twelve months, which is risky.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Candidate B, the Digital Archive, repeats the failed digitisation project from six years ago.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate C, the Maker Workshop, lacks certified tool technicians, which is a safety and skill gap.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, do you think the road closure risk is manageable for the Mobile Branch?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, the community halls kept their timetables despite closures, so it might be feasible.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"I am leaning towards A, but the funding structure worries me.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,I strongly oppose B because we already have the records of its failure.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I am hesitant about C because of the supervision issue, but the volunteers are helpful.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"The delivery windows for scanning are bad, but the mobile vehicle is already in the fleet.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"The attendance data for outreach was strong, supporting the Mobile Branch idea.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,The grant terms for A are too short-term; we need a more stable model.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"The partner-run groups for A are still active, which is a positive sign for sustainability.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"The volunteer register shows we have the people for C, but not the training.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I will vote for D, as the road risk is lower than I initially thought.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I will vote for D, as it solves the access problem in the outer wards.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"I will vote for A, as the partner groups provide some stability despite the grant issue.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"I will vote for A, as the partner-run model has proven successful in the past.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I will vote for C, as the volunteer base is strong and we can address the training gap.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
